            <Placemark id="43">
                <name>Wentzville Ice Arena (City of Wentzville Parks &amp; Recreation) - snow-load roof/wall collapse (Wentzville, MO)</name>
                <description>Social Media | has contact: Yes
NEW this report
storm damage to commercial/industrial roof (heavy wet snow - roof and two walls collapsed) | Open - storm-damaged roof | 2026-11-27 (Hard Hat Report published 11/27; follow-ups from KMOV/Gray News and Spectrum News 11/27; first reported 11/26 by STLPR/FOX 2 - not listed in any prior run)
Heavy, wet Thanksgiving snow (6-8") collapsed part of the roof and two walls of the east rink at the city-owned Wentzville Ice Arena (67,800 SF, two NHL rinks, opened 1998) between 3-4 AM 11/26; building declared uninhabitable, facility closed, mayor calls it a "total loss" and says the city will rebuild (Board of Aldermen approval needed). NWS St. Louis LSR also logged the collapse.
Contact: Mike Lueck, Parks and Recreation Director (also Roy Hays, Asst. Director (636) 639-2087; Ryan Motts, Ice Arena Operations (636) 639-7602)
Phone: (636) 639-2080
Email: Mike.Lueck@wentzvillemo.gov
Can solicit: Yes (Licensed/registered)
Armour is licensed or registered here (general info, not legal advice)
Website: https://www.wentzvillemo.gov
Confidence: High (official City of Wentzville staff directory). Public owner - rebuild likely goes through city procurement
Source: https://hardhatreport.com/story/wentzville-ice-arena-roof-collapse/ ; https://www.stlpr.org/news-briefs/2026-11-26/thanksgiving-snowstorm-collapses-wentzville-ice-arena-mayor-calls-total-loss
~317 mi from Omaha</description>
                <styleUrl>#44</styleUrl>
                <Point id="42">
                    <coordinates>-90.8525,38.8199,0.0</coordinates>
                </Point>
            </Placemark>
            <Placemark id="48">
                <name>SpringHill Suites by Marriott St. Louis Chesterfield - partial collapse under snow load (Chesterfield, MO)</name>
                <description>Social Media | has contact: Yes
NEW this report
storm damage to commercial/industrial roof (snow load - partial building collapse) | Open - storm-damaged building | 2026-11-27 (Hoodline published 11/27; FOX 2 first reported 11/26 5:10 PM CST - not listed in any prior run)
Part of the SpringHill Suites by Marriott in Chesterfield came down under the weight of the snow around 3:40 AM 11/26; debris blocked the main entrance and several windows; no injuries reported. Extent of the structural damage and cause not yet confirmed officially.
Contact: Hotel front desk / general manager (ownership/management company not identified)
Phone: (636) 519-7500
Email: -
Can solicit: Yes (Licensed/registered)
Armour is licensed or registered here (general info, not legal advice)
Website: https://www.marriott.com/en-us/hotels/stlsu-springhill-suites-st-louis-chesterfield/overview/
Confidence: Medium (official Marriott property page; hotel main line - ask for GM/ownership group; address 1065 Chesterfield Pkwy E, Census geocoder match)
Source: https://hoodline.com/2026/11/snow-load-caves-in-part-of-chesterfield-marriott-before-thanksgiving-dawn/ ; https://fox2now.com/news/missouri/part-of-chesterfield-hotel-collapses-under-weight-of-snow/
~337 mi from Omaha</description>
